		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Re: Receiving DMR Signal But No Audio]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4868&amp;p=36672#p36672"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div><blockquote class="uncited"><div><blockquote class="uncited"><div><br><br>Duplex hotspots and DMR seems to be tricky, I have one that works fine with D-Star but running a TDMA protocol with two timeslots seems<br>to be much more sensitive.<br>And our 70 cm band in the Nordic countries is only 432-438 MHz which makes it difficult to get TX/RX separation , especially if you follow the<br>bandplan where the repeater shift is 2 MHz.</div></blockquote><br>The more than 5Mhz separation is suggested on Dual HS in order to avoid issues on ADF7021 ICs.<br>Any other "dual" nodes, don't need to follow that suggestion if good quality resonant splitter used on RX/TX radios.<br>Obviously 2Mhz shift is hard and expensive to get property working anyway not impossible.<br><br>Maybe a special request to admin for those situations will help you getting more than 2Mhz...</div></blockquote>With "admin" you mean the Swedish Telecommunication authorities ?<br>I doubt they would care about such request, they are not so amateur radio friendly.<br><br>Anyway it's no big deal , I adjusted the oscillator on the MMDVM Dual HS  with my GPSDO referenced  frequency counter now so it much better.<br>BER is down into the "green area" and no "Timeout" on TX anymore.<br><br>And I noticed that a TG4000 Unlink have no effect when someone is talking on the TS ( TG91) anyway which would have been a "feature" sometimes <img class="smilies" src="http://localhost/opengd77/images/smilies/icon_e_smile.gif" width="15" height="17" alt=":)" title="Smile"></div></blockquote>Unlink command mist be sent when your system is not receiving not RF nor network.<br><br>At this point, in Pi-Star or WPSD, for BM is quite useful to have the API KEY installed. This allows you to MUTE the current talker and being free to TG4000 keying.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=101">EA3FA</a> — Wed Apr 09, 2025 7:38 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
