<blockquote class="uncited"><div><br>Duplex hotspots and DMR seems to be tricky, I have one that works fine with D-Star but running a TDMA protocol with two timeslots seems<br>to be much more sensitive.<br>And our 70 cm band in the Nordic countries is only 432-438 MHz which makes it difficult to get TX/RX separation , especially if you follow the<br>bandplan where the repeater shift is 2 MHz.</div></blockquote>Yep, totally agreed, I've tried 10 MHz shift, still have de-sensitization issues. I've a thought of doing notch filter and duplexer to make the hotspot act more like the repeater, but it seems too much. I ended up config it to run as simplex.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=5068">KA1CM</a> — Wed Feb 12, 2025 2:33 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
